  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards TB/HIV Epidemic Control in Malawi: Bringing Innovations to Scale - Malawi (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malawi, TB/HIV, ActionAid International Malawi (AA)This program has the following goals: Reduce HIV-related morbidity and mortality.  Reduce morbidity and mortality from tuberculosis.  Reduce the number of new infections towards elimination of HIV transmission by 2030. The objectives of this program are: 90% of diagnosed PLHIV are on ART.  90% of PLHIV know their status.  90% of PLHIV on ART are virally suppressed.  Increase case finding of RR/MDR TB to 60%.  Increase TB case notification to 191/ 100000.  Increase Treatment success of bacteriolgically confirmed TB case to 88%.  Reduce the number of new HIV infections among key and vulnerable populations</narrative>
  </description>
